From 6b26dbcc09435fad413f12a4a1e7bd20e6fe1ab5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ben Walker <ben@nvidia.com>
Date: Thu, 17 Sep 2026 08:20:33 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 07/17] sock: update release documentation

Update CHANGELOG.md and deprecation.md for the recent sock library changes.

Change-Id: If14f7bf54df730b13b146c0523d2dcf6e0337501
Signed-off-by: Ben Walker <ben@nvidia.com>
---
 CHANGELOG.md   |  9 +++++++++
 deprecation.md | 15 +++------------
 2 files changed, 12 insertions(+), 12 deletions(-)

diff --git a/CHANGELOG.md b/CHANGELOG.md
index c82caa78a..e8a69505e 100644
--- a/CHANGELOG.md
+++ b/CHANGELOG.md
@@ -128,6 +128,12 @@ larger MSDBD on HCAs that support more SGL entries, at the cost of a larger
 
 Removed the deprecated `spdk_sock_group_poll_count()` API. Use `spdk_sock_group_poll()` instead.
 
+`spdk_sock_connect`, `spdk_sock_connect_ext` and `spdk_sock_connect_async` have been collapsed
+into a single `spdk_sock_connect()`, as announced in v26.05. The replacement is always
+asynchronous: it returns the socket before the connection completes and reports the outcome
+through the supplied callback. Callers that need to block until the connection is established
+should poll `spdk_sock_is_connected()`.
+
 ## v26.05
 
 ### accel
@@ -366,6 +372,9 @@ removed in v26.09:
   `spdk_sock_group_provide_buf`, `spdk_sock_group_get_buf`) will be replaced by a new
   zero-copy API.
 
+The uring sock implementation no longer supports `enable_recv_pipe`; the option is accepted as
+a no-op for uring and only applies to posix/ssl.
+
 ### trace
 
 The shared-memory trace file (`spdk_trace_file`) was reorganized into a sequence of typed sections
diff --git a/deprecation.md b/deprecation.md
index a19e03ea1..656b9d9a4 100644
--- a/deprecation.md
+++ b/deprecation.md
@@ -115,16 +115,7 @@ removed in v27.01. Use `discovery_filters` instead.
 
 ### sock
 
-#### `spdk_sock_group_add_sock`, `spdk_sock_group_create`
+#### uring `enable_recv_pipe`
 
-The `cb_fn` and `cb_arg` parameters of `spdk_sock_group_add_sock` are deprecated and will be
-removed in v26.09. Instead, pass `cb_fn` and `cb_arg` via the new `spdk_sock_group_opts` struct
-passed to `spdk_sock_group_create`.
-
-#### `spdk_sock_connect`, `spdk_sock_connect_ext`, `spdk_sock_connect_async`
-
-These 3 APIs will be collapsed into a single replacement starting in v26.09.
-
-#### `spdk_sock_listen`, `spdk_sock_listen_ext`
-
-These two APIs will be collapsed into a single replacement starting in v26.09.
+`enable_recv_pipe` is no longer used by the uring sock implementation. The option remains
+accepted by `spdk_sock_impl_set_opts`, but it is a no-op for uring and only applies to posix/ssl.
